{
  "analysis": "Both test suites now pass. The first covered multiple dates per line, look-alike date strings, impossible calendar dates, and out of range octets. The second confirmed that Feb 29 is accepted, that an octet with a leading zero disqualifies the address, and that dates embedded in or adjacent to alphanumeric runs are ignored. The only capturing group in the pattern is the date, which is what re.findall will return.",
  "plan": "Nothing further is required. The finished expression is already saved in /app/regex.txt and has been verified against the described usage.",
  "task_complete": true
}
